bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    profile_hir_workers_linux_pin_rejects_dynamic_elf_2026-11-12, 0, "2026-11-12 fix-implemented. After #8663 the Linux HIR owner fails at the next gate: rt_process_pin_executable admitted only static ELF (rt_hal_static_elf_fd refused PT_INTERP/PT_DYNAMIC since 98215e0f708) and the Stage 2/3 compilers are dynamic (ld-linux + libc/libm/libstdc++/libgcc_s), so every Linux HIR pool started no worker (reason: owned executable pin was rejected). Fix: rt_hal_pinnable_elf_fd admits the system-loader dynamic class (Darwin parity: main image sealed + digest-bound; root-owned absolute PT_INTERP, no RPATH/RUNPATH, bare-soname DT_NEEDED), the Linux pov4 launch refuses LD_* environment, each admission prints one [rt-pin] stderr line. Evidence: doc/08_tracking/bug/profile_hir_workers_linux_pin_rejects_dynamic_elf_2026-11-12.md."
    profile_hir_workers_linux_pin_rejects_dynamic_elf_2026-11-12, 1, "2026-11-13 run 18 (b26b93aa54d): the C fix was never linked. Stage 2 links the Rust runtime crate (libsimple_native_all.a), whose build.rs compiles runtime_process_owned.c but never runtime_process.c, so cfg(not(macos)) Rust stubs in compiler_rust/runtime/src/value/sffi/env_process.rs answered -1 for every Linux pin (nm: rt_process_pin_executable_owned_value defined by a simple_runtime rcgu object; no simple-rthal string in the binary). Fix: the Linux pin, owned table, acquire, digest and close moved into runtime_process_owned.c beside the Darwin pin; the Rust stubs exclude Linux; seal constants defined locally (the crate TU has no _GNU_SOURCE, which had made the pin compile to return -1). Also fixed: the pin digest used a private SHA-256 copy with 63 round constants (0xc76c51a3 missing), now owned_sha256_block. Needs run 19."

